2: // Phase 5 T8 (FR-001, FR-002, FR-003, BR-002, BR-003): the signed-in user's
3: // durable outbox of text/reply messages and its ordered automatic delivery.
4: //
5: // - enqueue(): writes the item to IndexedDB (committed, strict durability)
6: //   BEFORE anything is dispatched and before the composer clears; a failed
7: //   write rejects with OutboxStorageError and nothing is sent (FR-033, D5).
8: // - Drain, per conversation, in creation order: only the oldest item is ever
9: //   eligible; one attempt at a time per conversation in this tab, and a Web
10: //   Lock per (owner, conversation) keeps other tabs of the browser from
11: //   draining the same conversation at the same time (released by the browser
12: //   when the tab closes or crashes). Leases, takeover of a hung holder,
13: //   cross-tab display and cancel are T10; explicit fencing of unknown items
14: //   and the 24 h window are T27/T9.
15: // - Every attempt carries a new attempt generation and the owner as
16: //   expectedSenderId. A generation-carrying create first fences every older
17: //   generation of the key on the server and replays a stored message (T2), so
18: //   redispatching an `unknown` or orphaned `claimed` item under the next
19: //   generation can never store a second copy.
20: // - Triggers: start (page load), enqueue, the browser `online` event, and a
21: //   capped backoff after a transient or unknown outcome.
22: // - An item is confirmed — removed from the outbox and its pending copy
23: //   dropped — by a 200/201/410 response, or the first time its stored key is
24: //   observed in the feed or Realtime (observeStoredMessages), whichever comes
25: //   first; a confirmed key is never shown again.
