longer commit) and never creates a message; the Phase 4 RPC `create_message_with_attachments` keeps its signature and 
delegates to the guarded function.
45: - Writes outside the fenced contract are refused at the database: `send_message_as_self` requires 
`client_message_id IS NULL` (client keyed inserts denied; unkeyed direct inserts still work); trigger 
`messages_client_message_id_immutable` refuses setting/changing/clearing a key or moving a keyed message to another 
conversation/sender for every role (42501); trigger `messages_keyed_insert_fence` fences raw keyed inserts (e.g. a 
Phase 4 server's service-role insert) — allowed only while the key has no fence state, else ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED — and 
records delivery.
46: - Every keyed message has a delivery record (backfill for existing keyed messages; fence/replay record untracked 
ones under the key lock); a keyed message deleted after this migration is never re-created (fence → `stored` with 
`message: null`; generation-carrying create → 410 MESSAGE_DELETED).
47: - `POST /api/messages/create` accepts `attemptGeneration` (≥1, requires key and expectedSenderId) and 
`expectedSenderId` (users.id; mismatch → 403 SENDER_MISMATCH before anything is read/stored/fenced); new `POST 
/api/messages/fence` (own key only; 401 anon; 200 stored|not_stored; 409 ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED for older generations; 403 
NOT_PARTICIPANT; never creates). Create/fence responses carry `clientMessageId` (top level and on `message`). Original 
composition stored per key (content, type, replyToId, sorted attachmentIds) for replay comparison; T4 adds sorted 
mention IDs.
